## UNMEASURED - stated rather than glossed

- No Schemathesis run. That the `positive_data_acceptance` no-body cases stop firing for `POST /api/nft/verify/transaction` and `POST /api/nft/verify/asset` is a prediction from the rendered spec (a `required: true` request body means a conforming generator no longer sends an empty one), not a measurement. A live re-check needs a running stack; KS-1380's build problem was reported for other services and was not re-measured here.
- The SERVED contract (`/api/docs/openapi.json` through the gateway) was not read; the gateway serves `docs/openapi/secuura-api.yaml`, so it needs the regenerated YAML to land (see Scope).
- That the handler answers 400 for an ABSENT body was read at source (a zod `object` rejects `undefined`/`{}`) and is what KS-1364's sweep 4 measured live (`status 400`); it was not re-run in-process here.
- node_modules: the workspace root is symlink-farmed from the `sparkfeed` checkout (installed at `94c9c7aa`); the nft-certificate service ALSO needs its own lock's modules (`@types/node` 20.19.39 vs the root farm's 26.1.0, which makes `tsc` fail rc 2 at the UNTOUCHED tip, three TS2322 in `ipfs.service.ts`); they were `npm ci --ignore-scripts`-installed into an isolated scratch dir from the tip's service lock and symlink-farmed into the clone; with them tsc is rc 0 at tip and golden. Between `94c9c7aa` and the tip the root lock moved (KS-1378's axios/dompurify refresh among others); zod, zod-to-openapi and vitest were not re-verified as identical to a fresh `npm ci` at the tip.
- The YAML companion was generated in this writer's scratch clone (`npm run generate-openapi`); it stacks with the other two KS-1364 carves' companions (measured: all three apply strictly in sequence). Whether it stacks with the KS-1015 envelope READY's own YAML companion was NOT measured (a different region of the file; expected to).

